{"postPage":{"id":"f5bcf904-63be-4055-97ba-0c081cbede71","post":{"id":"f5bcf904-63be-4055-97ba-0c081cbede71","title":"Salt Baked Whole Fish","excerpt":"Salt Baked Whole Fish Baking a whole fish encrusted in salt makes a very impressive yet very simple meal to prepare for a feast.  A feast...","firstPublishedDate":"2017-11-24T17:24:50.073Z","lastPublishedDate":"2017-11-24T17:24:50.073Z","url":{"base":"https://www.theglasspantry.com","path":"/single-post/2017/11/25/salt-baked-whole-fish"},"slug":"2017/11/25/salt-baked-whole-fish","featured":false,"pinned":false,"categoryIds":["15abe877-7a05-4ea7-9f92-bfe7c73120b4","accdf66c-0e8c-4ccb-9d3c-46a7d67e90f5","86cb13c9-ebe8-4da9-92bc-d9f63db5b610","6ba8db7a-6fe2-4b5a-83bf-acd0b1cbda4c"],"memberId":"2d3dcba5-39de-4c33-b11a-89d9248a0e51","hashtags":[],"commentingEnabled":true,"postCountInfo":{"comments":0,"likes":0,"views":186},"minutesToRead":3,"tagIds":["133312f6-2783-42cc-a99d-5c1c2da85922","5d9239d1-2d87-4018-989c-1d9077891496","4301b564-eeb4-442c-b1e2-b2f053070ee6","8c655a56-d3a9-4316-ab5d-4d722989a57c","53e2d91c-bdb5-433b-9f72-7ef07c0f8fe8","e4f7b387-fa56-4ee5-87fe-7d0a55071e05"],"relatedPostIds":[],"pricingPlanIds":[],"language":"en","metrics":{"comments":0,"likes":0,"views":186,"totalRatings":0,"averageRating":0},"seoData":{"tags":[{"type":"title","children":"Salt Baked Whole Fish","custom":false,"disabled":false},{"type":"meta","props":{"name":"description","content":"Salt Baked Whole Fish | Baked Whole Fish | Parrot Fish"},"children":"","custom":false,"disabled":false}]},"richContent":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"3iu0p","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"1u189","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"HEADING","id":"25bek","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Salt Baked Whole Fish","decorations":[]}}],"headingData":{"level":2,"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"1dru6","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"fnvqj","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_83af95ba3a9b4aaa8da8329afb22d7ca~mv2.jpg"},"width":1500,"height":1004},"altText":""}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"cqc62","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" Baking a whole fish encrusted in salt makes a very impressive yet very simple meal to prepare for a feast.  A feast for the eyes as well as the stomach and don't worry, because the fish has it's skin and scales intact, it will never absorb too much salt. Any cleaned whole fish with scales still on will work but this has got to be the most beautiful fish I've ever prepared. It's called a Parrot Fish and this one was from Vietnam, although this species can be found in many different places in the world.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"9qnkn","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"2rt60","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"I purchased this frozen and I was really impressed with the quality. Even though it had been in my freezer for a few months it was wonderful! I was amazed at how clear the eyes were when we thawed it out in the refrigerator overnight. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"148sb","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"14sa8","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" The fish was whole and had not been cleaned in any way so my hubby cleaned the fish but left the scales on. I made up a quick batch of the baking salt mixture and cut up a lemon and some rosemary and that's all there is to it. You could salt and pepper the inside of the fish but I didn't. I hadn't had Parrot Fish before so I didn't want to cover the flavor of the fish too much and I guess that was the right thing to do because this is a very mild fish. It seemed almost like a very large rainbow trout from the ocean. I love the briny smell of fresh ocean fish and this smelled wonderful before and after cooking it. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"3dspu","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"ap1s","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fqer6","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"3q9k0","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"We had invited some friends over last week and I had been waiting to prepare this fish until we had a group joining us for dinner because the fish was so large (almost 3 pounds). It seemed the perfect time. Especially because one of my friends is from Vietnam and she loves fish! She was so excited when we opened the salt casing to revealed this beautiful fish. She immediately went to work decorating it for serving with a bunch of cherry tomatoes still ripening on my kitchen counter. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fednf","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"am19e","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"In Vietnam, this is the kind of meal served family style at the table with some ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Nuoc Cham","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700},{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"foreground":"#0957a2"}},{"type":"LINK","linkData":{"link":{"url":"www.theglasspantry.com/single-post/2017/10/16/Quick-and-Easy-Nuoc-Cham","target":"BLANK"}}}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" so I made some of that to go with it. The interesting thing she told me was that in Vietnam when they made this kind of whole baked fish, they used clay mud instead of salt. I wonder if that seasons the fish with any different mineral tastes depending on where you get the mud?","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"38tfq","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"flkjs","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"2mnjb","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_7d8f5228df0f484595ab93c578251007~mv2.jpg"},"width":1125,"height":1500},"altText":"Whole Fish Baked in Salt"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5mfvh","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" The Reveal!","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700},{"type":"ITALIC","italicData":true}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5btu6","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"8ecn9","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fugqa","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"9g1ol","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Here is a short slide show showing how I put this together.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"153vg","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"9ebma","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"GALLERY","id":"6gjjt","nodes":[],"galleryData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"items":[{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_9dcc876a0abc4311bc9d9e2fa9088e89~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024}},"title":"Mixing the salt"},{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_5343d62dfd9547a1b544b59900ff3187~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024}},"title":"Salt mixed for baking."},{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_b4ac618af4d14772825a8dc7d46db7eb~mv2.jpg"},"width":1500,"height":1125}},"title":"Beautiful Parrot Fish"},{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_e7a4c87c243d4ae4a4dd4d9487ac102a~mv2.jpg"},"width":1500,"height":1125}},"title":"Ready to stuff."},{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_3ca5f8a636224cf385c856ed35dacd0b~mv2.jpg"},"width":1420,"height":1065}},"title":"Parrot Fish"},{"image":{"media":{"src":{"url":"577c92_0771159481c143f69d2f4ec81ae154bc~mv2.jpg"},"width":873,"height":641}},"title":"Cover the fish."}],"options":{"layout":{"type":"FULLSIZE","horizontalScroll":false,"orientation":"ROWS","numberOfColumns":3},"item":{"targetSize":300,"ratio":1,"crop":"FILL","spacing":10},"thumbnails":{"placement":"BOTTOM","spacing":0}}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"2do55","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"feiqk","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"52g0e","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"bfi6v","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"After removing the baked fish from the oven I let it sit on the counter for 10 minutes.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"c1vhi","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"7ti25","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_2590cd16090442b1b81ffa443dab35ca~mv2.jpg"},"width":1500,"height":1125},"altText":"Whole Fish Baked in S